1
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,900
"The Missing Piece"

2
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:51,800
(Episode 10)

3
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,560
Why are you back?

4
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,639
I was gonna ask you the same.

5
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,960
Didn't you say you went back home?

6
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:14,919
Why are you here all alone?

7
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,080
Ah.

8
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,719
Well, my parents

9
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,440
decided to go on a trip last minute.

10
00:02:20,759 --> 00:02:22,680
So I came back early.

11
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,920
Don't tell me you spent New Year's alone.

12
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,320
This is all you ate last night?

13
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:44,319
Mm.

14
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,120
Shen Mo.

15
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:52,800
Come here.

16
00:03:34,159 --> 00:03:34,879
Didn't you say

17
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,520
you were staying abroad a few more days?

18
00:03:37,719 --> 00:03:39,039
Why are you back so soon?

19
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,439
Something urgent came up.

20
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:47,319
Changed my plans.

21
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,800
What was it?

22
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,400
You know full well.

23
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,800
How did you know
I didn't go back home？

24
00:03:56,759 --> 00:03:57,759
That I spent New Year's alone?

25
00:03:58,319 --> 00:04:00,039
I figured it out when we talked last night.

26
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:03,159
A bit late.

27
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:05,879
Not too late.

28
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,872
Tickets must've be hard to book in such a hurry.

29
00:04:11,599 --> 00:04:12,599
Anything can be solved

30
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,080
with money.

31
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,319
There are problems money can't solve.

32
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:19,959
There are.

33
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,120
Such as...

34
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,279
how to make someone fall for me.

35
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:34,519
Isn't my love enough for you?

36
00:04:35,639 --> 00:04:36,959
Who else do you want to love you?

37
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:42,199
Say it again.

38
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,079
I like you.

39
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,720
Shh.

40
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,240
Don't make a sound.

41
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,480
Give it to me.

42
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,920
Okay?

43
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,480
No.

44
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,639
It's too tight.

45
00:07:12,639 --> 00:07:13,639
Don't go.

46
00:07:13,839 --> 00:07:15,040
Please.

47
00:07:18,439 --> 00:07:19,439
I love you.

48
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,639
You asked for this.

49
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,959
Did it hurt just now?

50
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,360
A little.

51
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:18,800
Give me your hand.

52
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,920
Mm.

53
00:08:20,752 --> 00:08:21,752
What for?

54
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,800
This is...

55
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,279
Your New Year gift.

56
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,280
I was busy and forgot earlier.

57
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,600
We've been married so long.

58
00:08:38,759 --> 00:08:40,559
Why so sappy?

59
00:08:40,792 --> 00:08:41,792
Huh?

60
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,279
You came back early.

61
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,639
Will your family mind?

62
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,200
Oh.

63
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,600
My sister, she...

64
00:08:47,659 --> 00:08:48,659
Your sister?

65
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,559
Aren't you an only child?

66
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,600
What about you?

67
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,280
You didn't go home for New Year.

68
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,640
You don't want to talk about it.

69
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,759
There's really no reason.

70
00:09:08,279 --> 00:09:09,279
It's just...

71
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:12,399
It's just my parents kicked me out again.

72
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,799
You know.

73
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,840
Last summer break.

74
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:17,679
I told them

75
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,200
about us.

76
00:09:19,679 --> 00:09:20,440
My family is

77
00:09:20,441 --> 00:09:21,879
pretty traditional.

78
00:09:22,039 --> 00:09:23,279
How could they ever accept it?

79
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,480
Especially my dad.

80
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,000
So...

81
00:09:27,559 --> 00:09:29,000
So now you're all alone.

82
00:09:30,399 --> 00:09:31,399
How could that be?

83
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,639
Don't I still have you?

84
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
What's wrong?

85
00:09:37,559 --> 00:09:39,120
We won't ever split up, right?

86
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,360
We won't split up, will we?

87
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Of course not.

88
00:09:50,639 --> 00:09:51,639
But...

89
00:09:53,032 --> 00:09:55,552
you need to dry your hair properly now.

90
00:09:56,639 --> 00:09:57,679
Or you'll get a headache.

91
00:10:38,639 --> 00:10:39,840
Ever since that day,

92
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,039
Zhou Yang has been sleeping with me.

93
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:46,960
Stop working.

94
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,279
Come to bed.

95
00:10:50,759 --> 00:10:51,759
Okay, okay, okay.

96
00:10:52,759 --> 00:10:53,759
Coming right up.

97
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:58,279
Put it down.

98
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:12,600
Oh man.

99
00:11:12,624 --> 00:11:13,904
Why were you so fierce just now?

100
00:11:14,885 --> 00:11:15,885
Is that not allowed?

101
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,278
Once my hand heals

102
00:11:23,279 --> 00:11:24,360
and I can draw again

103
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,279
I'll go find a job drawing.

104
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:27,919
Then I'll take care of you.

105
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,440
You'll take care of me?

106
00:11:33,759 --> 00:11:34,759
Mm.

107
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,120
Okay, okay.

108
00:11:43,799 --> 00:11:45,279
I'll wait for you to take care of me.

109
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,799
I'm back at our old home.

110
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Graduation photo.

111
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:22,320
Isn't Yang in the graduation photo?

112
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,159
Who am I in this photo with?

113
00:14:38,159 --> 00:14:39,320
That's not Yang.

114
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:40,279
Or rather.

115
00:14:40,679 --> 00:14:43,240
This isn't
the Yang I spent every day with.

116
00:14:43,845 --> 00:14:44,966
Then who is this person?

117
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,159
If this person isn't Yang

118
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,440
why did I have so much contact with him?

119
00:15:00,639 --> 00:15:02,440
But if this person is Yang...

120
00:15:24,039 --> 00:15:25,039
Yang.

121
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,480
You're back.

122
00:15:27,039 --> 00:15:28,039
I'm not Yang.

123
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,760
And of course Yang won't come back.

124
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,200
Keep running away.

125
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:35,879
Or wake up and face reality.

126
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,039
Your choice.

127
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:39,159
Yang.

128
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,679
Yang, come back.

129
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,360
Yang went abroad.

130
00:15:47,759 --> 00:15:48,759
He's not coming back.

131
00:15:51,039 --> 00:15:52,480
You should start a new life.

132
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:55,960
I'm glad you're back.

133
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
You.

134
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,080
Why are you here.

135
00:16:19,799 --> 00:16:20,799
Oh.

136
00:16:21,399 --> 00:16:22,719
Nothing much at the office today.

137
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,200
So I came to see you.

138
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:32,679
You're painting again.

139
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,080
Mm.

140
00:16:35,639 --> 00:16:36,639
It's really good.

141
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,840
What's wrong?

142
00:16:45,919 --> 00:16:47,000
Why are your hands so cold?

143
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,480
Are you too tired?

144
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:50,840
Mm.

145
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,960
I know you want to paint again.

146
00:16:54,039 --> 00:16:55,399
But don't push yourself too hard.

147
00:16:57,039 --> 00:16:58,279
Just take it easy.

148
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,880
Are you done?

149
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,680
If you are,

150
00:17:09,805 --> 00:17:10,926
let's go home.

151
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:18,839
Okay.

152
00:17:20,559 --> 00:17:21,640
He's not Zhou Yang.

153
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,559
Who is this person I see every day?

154
00:17:32,079 --> 00:17:33,079
Shen Mo.

155
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,400
Your birthday is in a few days.

156
00:17:38,433 --> 00:17:39,553
How do you want to spend it?

157
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,079
I just spend my birthday
casually every year.

158
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:45,119
No need to go out of your way.

159
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:49,879
Then I'll take care of it.

160
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,759
He even knows my birthday.

161
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,279
How could he not be Zhou Yang?

162
00:17:59,599 --> 00:18:00,599
But if...

163
00:18:01,079 --> 00:18:02,440
If he's not Zhou Yang,

164
00:18:03,266 --> 00:18:04,906
why pretend to be Zhou Yang?

165
00:18:04,930 --> 00:18:06,370
And why be so good to me?

166
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,400
What's wrong?

167
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,480
Not feeling well?

168
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:13,200
Mm

169
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,559
I feel a bit cold.

170
00:19:17,598 --> 00:19:20,960
Based on your reports, you're
recovering well, there aren't any problems.

171
00:19:21,279 --> 00:19:22,839
Just keep taking your meds.

172
00:19:28,279 --> 00:19:29,279
Doctor.

173
00:19:30,519 --> 00:19:31,839
This condition of mine.

174
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,960
Could it make me mistake someone?

175
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:37,759
Mistake someone?

176
00:19:39,913 --> 00:19:40,913
Like...

177
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:44,621
Taking a stranger and seeing
them as someone very close.

178
00:19:46,839 --> 00:19:51,319
People with severe psychological trauma
usually choose to escape themselves.

179
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,359
They actively forget
certain things and people.

180
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,240
But as for mistaking someone...

181
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:59,240
That depends on the situation.

182
00:20:01,039 --> 00:20:02,039
Oh.

183
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,519
I understand.

184
00:20:03,559 --> 00:20:04,559
Mm.

185
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:23,720
Hello.

186
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,799
The number you dialed
is temporarily unavailable.

187
00:20:27,319 --> 00:20:28,559
Please try again later.

188
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,880
Sorry the subscriber
you dialed can not be...

189
00:21:33,759 --> 00:21:34,839
I figured you'd be here.

190
00:21:39,759 --> 00:21:40,759
Yeah.

191
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:43,960
Where else would I be?

192
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:50,440
Were you waiting for me?

193
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,200
Yes.

194
00:21:58,839 --> 00:21:59,839
And no.

195
00:22:15,759 --> 00:22:17,039
Today's your birthday.

196
00:22:19,799 --> 00:22:20,960
Why didn't you go home?

197
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,759
I'm thinking about some things.

198
00:22:30,505 --> 00:22:31,505
What things?

199
00:22:34,599 --> 00:22:35,680
Things from the past.

200
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:42,839
Can you tell me...

201
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:46,359
what exactly happened before?

202
00:22:49,039 --> 00:22:50,039
Yang.

203
00:22:53,079 --> 00:22:54,079
You're not Yang.

204
00:22:59,079 --> 00:23:00,160
Who are you really?

205
00:23:06,119 --> 00:23:07,119
Right.

206
00:23:09,359 --> 00:23:10,400
I'm not Yang.

207
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,599
Never was.

208
00:23:17,519 --> 00:23:18,480
Since you're not Yang,

209
00:23:18,481 --> 00:23:19,679
why are you pretending to be him?

210
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,799
I'm pretending to be him?

211
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,799
Weren't you the one who mistook me first?

212
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:29,799
Then you could've just left me alone.

213
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,759
Let me fend for myself.

214
00:23:33,359 --> 00:23:35,239
Or if you were feeling kind, you
could've just dumped me at a hospital.

215
00:23:35,263 --> 00:23:36,703
Why pretend to be Yang?

216
00:23:40,279 --> 00:23:42,480
At first I was afraid you'd
starve to death in this room.

217
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:46,240
So I dropped by now and then.

218
00:23:47,559 --> 00:23:48,200
Later I learned

219
00:23:48,201 --> 00:23:50,000
you're stubborn and headstrong.

220
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,759
And I worried even more.

221
00:23:54,279 --> 00:23:55,079
And then...

222
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,160
And then what?

223
00:23:57,359 --> 00:23:58,359
And then what?

224
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:16,400
Do you really not know?

225
00:24:19,119 --> 00:24:20,480
Why I stayed?

226
00:24:22,839 --> 00:24:23,839
Stop it.

227
00:24:31,359 --> 00:24:32,559
Because I like you.

228
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:35,720
Mo.

229
00:24:57,119 --> 00:24:58,119
A couple days ago

230
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:01,480
the doctor called me.

231
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,080
I already knew you were about to recover.

232
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,359
So you knew all along.

233
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,280
You were just lying to me the whole time.

234
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,320
Waking up is a good thing, actually.

235
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,839
You can't live in memories forever.

236
00:25:25,799 --> 00:25:26,799
Mo.

237
00:25:29,079 --> 00:25:30,160
Pack your things.

238
00:25:32,599 --> 00:25:33,680
Come home with me.

239
00:25:35,839 --> 00:25:36,960
This is my home.

240
00:25:37,319 --> 00:25:38,880
But we've lived together for so long.

241
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:42,039
No.

242
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:43,480
Why?

243
00:25:48,599 --> 00:25:49,599
You're not Yang.

244
00:25:54,079 --> 00:25:55,680
I'm waiting here for Yang to come back.

245
00:25:59,559 --> 00:26:00,720
Yang is abroad.

246
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:08,119
And you two broke up long ago.

247
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:09,279
No.

248
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:12,720
Yang and I just took a break, that's all.

249
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:14,920
Mo.

250
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,440
What about me?

251
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,599
I thought you were Yang.

252
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:31,319
He's the one I've always loved.

253
00:26:53,640 --> 00:26:54,640
I'm sorry.

254
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:00,680
Yang is the one you love.

255
00:27:04,519 --> 00:27:05,519
I'm sorry.

256
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:11,920
I shouldn't have come into your life.

257
00:27:38,839 --> 00:27:39,839
I'm giving this back to you.

258
00:28:50,920 --> 00:28:52,279
It was meant for you anyway.

259
00:28:54,759 --> 00:28:56,119
No point in me keeping it.

260
00:29:15,839 --> 00:29:16,880
After that

261
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:19,880
he never showed up in front of me again...

262
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:23,119
like we never had anything
to do with each other.

263
00:29:35,445 --> 00:29:38,112
["Happy Birthday" with an
address written underneath]

264
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:40,519
He actually gave me that house.

265
00:29:41,119 --> 00:29:43,000
I believe he was sincere with me.

266
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:46,039
I just want to sort
things out with Yang first

267
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:48,480
before thinking about him and me.

268
00:29:50,319 --> 00:29:51,319
That man.

269
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:53,119
Where could he be now?

270
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:55,320
Waiting for me at Jinxiu Mountain Villa?

271
00:29:56,359 --> 00:29:57,559
How long would he wait?

272
00:29:58,519 --> 00:29:59,519
A week?

273
00:30:00,039 --> 00:30:01,039
A month?

274
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:02,960
Or longer?

275
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:05,920
Zhou Yang.

276
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:11,400
Where are you?

277
00:30:17,512 --> 00:30:18,799
Hello?

278
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:20,240
Old Zhang?

279
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:21,400
Ah.

280
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,440
Um.

281
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:24,160
Have you seen Zhou Yang lately?

282
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:26,440
Zhou Yang.

283
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,720
Haven't heard from him since graduation.

284
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:30,439
Oh, okay.

285
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:30,799
Alright.

286
00:30:30,799 --> 00:30:31,759
No worries, it's fine.

287
00:30:31,759 --> 00:30:32,759
Sorry to bother you.

288
00:30:36,933 --> 00:30:37,933
Hey.

289
00:30:38,180 --> 00:30:39,660
Have you seen Yang lately?

290
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,400
No idea, no idea.

291
00:30:41,519 --> 00:30:42,519
Kind of busy.

292
00:30:50,799 --> 00:30:51,039
Right.

293
00:30:51,039 --> 00:30:51,680
Let me ask you something.

294
00:30:51,681 --> 00:30:53,599
Have you seen Yang around lately?

295
00:30:54,319 --> 00:30:56,519
I heard he went abroad.

296
00:30:56,559 --> 00:30:57,559
Ah.

297
00:30:57,839 --> 00:30:58,839
Then never mind.

298
00:31:09,599 --> 00:31:11,559
That person said Yang went abroad too.

299
00:31:12,319 --> 00:31:15,640
So me and Yang just ended
like this, with no explanation.

300
00:31:40,839 --> 00:31:42,720
Back when Yang and I rented this place,

301
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:46,505
Yang said he found someone
to handle the paperwork.

302
00:31:47,759 --> 00:31:48,920
Said it'd be easier that way.

303
00:31:49,319 --> 00:31:50,480
So no one could trace it.

304
00:31:52,079 --> 00:31:53,335
Sure enough, his surname is
Fang [TN: Full name Fang Yanzhou]

305
00:31:53,359 --> 00:31:55,759
I remember Yang always
called him Uncle Fang.

306
00:31:56,079 --> 00:31:57,839
He works for their Zhou Group.

307
00:32:06,759 --> 00:32:08,319
This is Zhou Yang's family business.

308
00:32:11,519 --> 00:32:11,920
Hello.

309
00:32:12,119 --> 00:32:12,519
Sir.

310
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:13,839
How can I help you?

311
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,000
I'm looking for this person.

312
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:18,758
You must mean Secretary Fang.

313
00:32:18,759 --> 00:32:20,078
His office is on the sixth floor.

314
00:32:20,079 --> 00:32:21,439
You can take the elevator.

315
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:21,759
Ah.

316
00:32:21,759 --> 00:32:22,079
Okay.

317
00:32:22,079 --> 00:32:22,519
Thank you.

318
00:32:22,519 --> 00:32:23,519
You're welcome.

319
00:32:25,680 --> 00:32:26,680
Hello, Mrs. Zhou.

320
00:32:34,832 --> 00:32:35,832
She...

321
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,200
why does she look so familiar?

322
00:32:40,359 --> 00:32:41,359
Hello, Mrs. Zhou.

323
00:32:42,319 --> 00:32:43,400
Mrs. Zhou.

324
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:44,480
Yang's mother.

325
00:32:45,519 --> 00:32:46,519
This time

326
00:32:46,839 --> 00:32:48,480
is just a warning.

327
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,518
Stay away from Yang from now on.

328
00:32:50,519 --> 00:32:51,519
You're not good enough for him.

329
00:32:52,559 --> 00:32:53,680
Leave Yang.

330
00:32:54,079 --> 00:32:55,079
Next time

331
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:57,559
your family will pay the price.

332
00:33:00,759 --> 00:33:01,759
I was kidnapped.

333
00:33:04,759 --> 00:33:05,759
Beaten.

334
00:33:07,759 --> 00:33:09,119
My fingers crushed.

335
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:12,519
Those weren't nightmares.

336
00:33:13,440 --> 00:33:15,359
They all really happened.

337
00:33:16,759 --> 00:33:17,759
Yang.

338
00:33:19,279 --> 00:33:20,440
Let's break up.

339
00:33:22,599 --> 00:33:23,160
No.

340
00:33:23,519 --> 00:33:25,119
This isn't our first meeting.

341
00:33:25,680 --> 00:33:26,960
Before the hospital

342
00:33:27,279 --> 00:33:28,519
I must have seen him before.

343
00:33:43,599 --> 00:33:44,599
I remember now.

344
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,440
He's...

345
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:49,099
his name is Ji Mingxuan.
